A||N||3||^-sHarK-^||Sprang a leak||||9||
Z||000000||^-sHarK-^||04-14-2000||07:45 PM||||Hello all,<P>I have an 86 SE, 2.8, 4 speed. On the way home from work today, I was sitting at a stoplight and noticed a little steam creeping up the crack behind the back window. I only had a mile to go to get home and the temp guage said every thing was still cool.  So, I pulled in the driveway and popped the trunk lid to see were all of the steam was coming from.  Looking down at the metal "inlet pipe", I saw my baby's precious yellow/green blood spewing  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> from the slightly curved elbow in the pipe. This is the pipe between the engine and firewall. It looks as though this pipe has had troubles in the past.  I have a Chilton repair manual (pn 7571 page 16 item #2), and looking at the picture, it is one whole pipe.  Over time someone has cut out a section and pieced it together with a short (4")section of hose. I think that the pipe is just rotten on the inside and is starting to give up the ghost.<P>I was wondering if this part is still available from Pontiac (or another source) or do I have to try my luck at the boneyard(..and who knows what condition it may be in)?<P>Thanks in advance.<BR>Charles<BR>||||reg||9
Z||000001||ka4nkf||04-14-2000||09:19 PM||||Check with rodney, I think he is going to supply these pipes.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rodney||04-15-2000||12:32 PM||||I have all the years and transmission type V-6 coolant crossover pipes in stock now. 1985-1988 automatic and manual.  Exact in size and correct bends. You may still be able to get the 85-87 pipe from GM? It will still be steel. Mine are 304 stainless steel. The 88 design is no longer available from GM. <P>On my web page: <A HREF="http://www.execpc.com/~rodney1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.execpc.com/~rodney1/</A> <P>Rodney Dickman||||reg||1
Z||000003||^-sHarK-^||04-15-2000||12:42 PM||||Thanks ka4nkf.  I went to Rodney's web page and checked things out.<P>Rodney,  Thanks for the info.  I sent you an email earlier this morning.<P>Charles||||reg||7
